            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Ginsburg asked whether the petitioner\u2019s basic position was that the Florida legislation violated the Takings Clause and why the focus shifted from the legislature to the judiciary."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9c5b75ef7ee888e72ddce64dfd4283758034c0194a481452b905e581fd921c08",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9c5b75ef7ee8-0000-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 6,
              "start": 6
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Scalia, justice Scalia questioned whether the right of contact with the water could be eliminated by an avulsion."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9c5b75ef7ee888e72ddce64dfd4283758034c0194a481452b905e581fd921c08",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9c5b75ef7ee8-0000-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 9,
              "start": 9
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Chief Justice Roberts asked whether a private party could be barred from placing a hot\u2011dog stand on newly created land."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9c5b75ef7ee888e72ddce64dfd4283758034c0194a481452b905e581fd921c08",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9c5b75ef7ee8-0000-0009"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 19,
              "start": 19
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Kennedy asked a question about Florida property valuation."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9c5b75ef7ee888e72ddce64dfd4283758034c0194a481452b905e581fd921c08",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9c5b75ef7ee8-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 40,
              "start": 40
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Scalia asked whether a person would still be considered a littoral owner after the state adds sand."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Alito",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9c5b75ef7ee888e72ddce64dfd4283758034c0194a481452b905e581fd921c08",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9c5b75ef7ee8-0002-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 41,
              "start": 41
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Alito, justice Alito posed a hypothetical about a city creating a large beach in front of privately owned homes for spring\u2011break tourists."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9c5b75ef7ee888e72ddce64dfd4283758034c0194a481452b905e581fd921c08",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9c5b75ef7ee8-0003-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 59,
              "start": 59
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Sotomayor asked whether there is a generally understood common\u2011law littoral right to contact the water."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9c5b75ef7ee888e72ddce64dfd4283758034c0194a481452b905e581fd921c08",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9c5b75ef7ee8-0003-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 60,
              "start": 60
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Chief Justice Roberts, chief Justice Roberts wondered whether adding an amusement park would be permissible under the petitioner\u2019s theory."
      }
    ],
