  "overview": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioner",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9c5b75ef7ee888e72ddce64dfd4283758034c0194a481452b905e581fd921c08",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9c5b75ef7ee8-0000-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 11,
              "start": 11
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The petitioner says the Florida legislature may redefine what counts as property, but if that definition results in a taking, the state must pay just compensation under the Takings Clause."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "MR. SAFRIET",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9c5b75ef7ee888e72ddce64dfd4283758034c0194a481452b905e581fd921c08",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9c5b75ef7ee8-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 21,
              "start": 21
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to MR. SAFRIET, the petitioner argues that the beach is actually gaining sand (accreting) rather than eroding, and there is about 200 feet of dry beach that is growing over time."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioner",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9c5b75ef7ee888e72ddce64dfd4283758034c0194a481452b905e581fd921c08",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9c5b75ef7ee8-0003-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 62,
              "start": 62
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The petitioner claims that owners have a right, under Florida common law and their deeds, to own land up to the mean high\u2011water line."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioner",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9c5b75ef7ee888e72ddce64dfd4283758034c0194a481452b905e581fd921c08",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9c5b75ef7ee8-0003-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 63,
              "start": 63
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Petitioner, the petitioner invokes the doctrine of reclamation, which allows a landowner to replace sand lost to the sea in order to re\u2011establish the mean high\u2011water line."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Overview",
    "status": "complete",
    "summary": null,
    "summary_citations": []
  },
  "party_positions": [
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "9c5b75ef7ee888e72ddce64dfd4283758034c0194a481452b905e581fd921c08",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-9c5b75ef7ee8-0000-0006"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 11,
                "start": 11
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "The petitioner argues that the legislature\u2019s redefinition of property must be accompanied by just compensation when it results in a taking."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "MR. SAFRIET",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "9c5b75ef7ee888e72ddce64dfd4283758034c0194a481452b905e581fd921c08",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-9c5b75ef7ee8-0001-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 21,
                "start": 21
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to MR. SAFRIET, the petitioner maintains that the beach is accreting, providing additional dry land rather than eroding existing property."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "9c5b75ef7ee888e72ddce64dfd4283758034c0194a481452b905e581fd921c08",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-9c5b75ef7ee8-0003-0003"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 62,
                "start": 62
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "The petitioner claims owners have rights to the mean high\u2011water line under Florida common law and their deeds."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "9c5b75ef7ee888e72ddce64dfd4283758034c0194a481452b905e581fd921c08",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-9c5b75ef7ee8-0003-0004"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 63,
                "start": 63
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioner, the petitioner invokes the doctrine of reclamation, allowing landowners to replace sand lost to the sea to restore the mean high\u2011water line."
        }
      ],
